BT 
/F1 10 Tf 
14 TL 
54 740 Td 
(ECP-2400 EMERGENCY COOLING PUMP SYSTEM - SAFETY, ELECTRICAL & STARTUP) Tj 
T* 
(Document ID: ECP-2400-OM-REV4 | Section 3: Commissioning Procedures) Tj 
T* 
() Tj 
T* 
(3. VIBRATION, THERMAL THRESHOLDS, ELECTRICAL SUPPLY & AIR BLEEDING) Tj 
T* 
() Tj 
T* 
(3.1 Vibration and Temperature Safety Thresholds) Tj 
T* 
(- Normal baseline overall vibration: below 2.2 mm/s RMS velocity.) Tj 
T* 
(- Cavitation warning threshold: vibration levels exceeding 4.5 mm/s RMS indicate severe cavitation;) Tj 
T* 
(  operators must immediately verify suction net positive suction head \(NPSH\) and throttle discharge.) Tj 
T* 
(- Emergency shutdown bearing temperature: 95 C \(alarm warning trips at 85 C; automatic trip at 95 C\).) Tj 
T* 
() Tj 
T* 
(3.2 Electrical Power Supply Requirements) Tj 
T* 
(- Power supply: 3-phase 400V AC at 50 Hz \(tolerance +/- 5%\).) Tj 
T* 
(- Motor power rating: 15 kW induction motor, rated full-load current 28.5 Amperes.) Tj 
T* 
() Tj 
T* 
(3.3 Mandatory Pre-Startup Air Bleeding Procedure) Tj 
T* 
(Before energizing the pump motor, all trapped air must be completely purged:) Tj 
T* 
(  Step 1: Open manual air vent valve V-2 located at the high point of the pump discharge casing.) Tj 
T* 
(  Step 2: Slowly crack open the suction line isolation valve to prime the impeller eye with fluid.) Tj 
T* 
(  Step 3: Allow liquid to displace trapped air until a solid, bubble-free fluid stream emerges from V-2.) Tj 
T* 
(  Step 4: Securely close manual vent valve V-2 and verify zero gland leakage prior to startup.) Tj 
T* 
ET
endstream
